From 7c9759c4fe05bedd32a4da354b655b7601ab370e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Mar 2026 08:35:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 198/213] WIP: media: rockchip: iep: Add Rockchip IEP2
 deinterlace driver

Add the V4L2 M2M driver for the Rockchip Image Enhancement Processor
v2 (IEP2) found in current RK35xx generation SoCs. IEP2 provides
hardware deinterlacing with motion detection, motion estimation, and
edge-directed interpolation.

The driver shares common V4L2 M2M framework code with the IEP(1)
driver via the iep-common module, implementing only the hardware
specific register programming, interrupt handling, clock management,
and DMA working buffer allocation.

Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
